// err_clear drops the count and the kept messages together: a pane showing
// sixteen stale diagnostics beside an input that now parses is worse than
// showing none.
//
// The last report is deliberate. It leaves the count at 1 so that main's return
// clause exits nonzero, which is what a muted program's only failure signal is.

t_clear() {
  err_clear();
  print("after err_clear: count exp 0 | nmsg exp 0 = " + err_count() + " " + err_nmsg());
  t_after();
} return void;

// Reporting still works after a clear -- the lists were emptied, not abandoned.
t_after() {
  err_report("e.id", 7, "still muted, still counted");
  print("one more while muted: count exp 1 | nmsg exp 1 | exit code will be 1 = " + err_count() + " " + err_nmsg());
} return void;
